cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, datasets, or methodology in your research or coursework, please cite it as below."
title: "Physics-Informed Solar Flare Early Warning Forecasting System"
abstract: "A machine learning pipeline for multi-horizon (5, 15, 30, and 60 minutes) solar flare forecasting using NOAA GOES-16/18 1-minute X-ray flux series (2022-2024 Solar Cycle 25 maximum) and the Archival Solar Flares (ASR) catalogue. Features physics-based clue groups (brightness dynamics, flare event history, quasi-periodic pulsation spectral ratios, and plasma phase transitions) evaluated under strict chronological validation with blackout buffers."
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/helio-unitov/ASR_cat"
keywords:
  - "solar flare forecasting"
  - "space weather"
  - "GOES XRS"
  - "machine learning"
  - "Heidke Skill Score"
  - "True Skill Statistic"
  - "quasi-periodic pulsations"
  - "solar cycle 25"

